.TITLE "mv"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Moves or renames files and directories. It changes the __location__ or the __name__ of a filesystem object without duplicating its data.

.DIV "TLDR"
**mv old_name new_name**
Renames a file or directory in its current location.
> __old_name__ current name | __new_name__ target name

**mv file.txt ~/Documents/**
Moves a specific file to a different directory.
> __file.txt__ source file | __~/Documents/__ target directory

**mv -v source destination**
Displays the name of each file or directory as it is being moved.
> __-v__ verbose flag

**mv -n source destination**
Prevents overwriting an existing file at the target destination.
> __-n__ no-clobber flag

**mv -i source destination**
Prompts for confirmation before overwriting an existing file.
> __-i__ interactive flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Because __mv__ is an atomic operation within the same filesystem, it is the fastest way to reorganize data. Use __-n__ or __-i__ to protect against accidental data loss when moving files into populated folders.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:cp** **mac:rm**

